! dcp_compool.strap -- the STRETCH MAINTENANCE COMPOOL, transcribed
! from ka_ua1_diagnostic_ctl_pgm.pdf PDF pp.129-130.  Page header, as
! printed: "@STRETCH MAINTENANCE COMPOOL, NOVEMBER 20, 1961".
!
! WHY THIS FILE EXISTS FIRST.  docs/archival_inventory.md calls these
! two pages "the single highest-leverage page in the whole find: the
! Rosetta stone that resolves symbols referenced by EVERY OTHER 7030
! diagnostic deck in bitsavers' diag/ directory, not just this one...
! without it, every other listing's symbols are dangling."  65 SYN
! entries, 51 on p.129 and 14 on p.130.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE.  This listing's pages carry no printed folios.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE OPERATOR PRINTS AS "&" AND IT IS ADDITION.  SUBSTITUTION 1.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every expression below prints in the listing as e.g.
! "SYN,ECTL1&.01", and at 600 dpi cropped to one column the glyph is
! unmistakably an ampersand -- closed lower loop, diagonal -- NOT a
! plus.  The MCP listing prints an ordinary "+" in the structurally
! identical place, so this is not simply how this project renders "+".
!
! IT WAS SETTLED BY ARITHMETIC, NOT BY LOOKING HARDER.  The page
! prints each expression AND its resolved address, so every row is its
! own oracle.  Reading the operator as addition, the offset as a
! DECIMAL bit count and the address column as OCTAL, 41 of the 41 rows
! that carry an offset come out exactly right (verify_dcp_compool.py).
!
! THE DECISIVE ROW IS MNTCTL.  It prints "SYN, ECTL2.62" -- with NO
! operator glyph at all -- and resolves to 4007.76, which is
! ECTL2 + 62 bits (0o76 = 62).  A row where the character is absent
! and the sum still holds is evidence about the operator that does not
! depend on reading the character.
!
! A HYPOTHESIS ABOUT *WHY*, AND NOTHING RESTS ON IT: the 12-zone punch
! prints "&" on BCDIC chains and "+" on EBCDIC ones, so a deck punched
! with "+" can print "&" on a different printer.  Recorded as a
! hypothesis.  The transcription rests on the 41-row check.
!
! SUBSTITUTION 2: the address column prints "4006.00&" and the binary
! column "&00000000", where MCP prints "+".  Nothing here reads those
! columns -- a SYN emits no code -- so they are not transcribed, and
! they are NOT silently normalised either.  Recorded as unexplained in
! docs/NEXT.md 5m.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "ETAP7" IS THE SYMBOL AS PRINTED, AND IT IS IBM'S OWN TYPO
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Between EQTAP6 and EQTAP8 the listing defines ETAP7, five characters
! where its neighbours have six.  Confirmed at 600 dpi: the symbol is
! not on a rule line and the Q is simply absent.  Kept as printed --
! any deck referring to it must spell it the same way -- and flagged
! here beside "PSEDUO" (ax5b_162_test3a) and "COUSE" (162_test1d) as a
! third deck typo this corpus preserves rather than corrects.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BASE SYMBOLS ARE DERIVED, AND THEY ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ECTL1-4, EQAV1-7 and EDCP1 are defined ELSEWHERE in the DCP, not on
! these two pages.  Their values below are back-computed from the
! printed addresses of the rows that use them, so for the twelve rows
! that carry no offset the address check is CIRCULAR BY CONSTRUCTION
! and proves nothing.  The 41 rows that carry an offset are genuine:
! they test the offset, the decimal-to-octal convention, and the
! operator reading.  This is the same rule the deck transcriptions
! state as "EVERY SYN IS AN INPUT TO THE CHECK, NOT A WITNESS".
!
! The rule-line trap (docs/listing_typography.md 10) is live on this
! page: a rule crossing a glyph can forge a bottom bar and turn F into
! E.  The prefix is settled by the rows that sit OFF the rules --
! EBAUTO, EMACH, ETAPDM, EDPLOC, EBHARV all begin with a clean E.

! ---- bases, DERIVED from the printed results (see header) ----------
ECTL1   SYN, (8)4006.0
ECTL2   SYN, (8)4007.0
ECTL3   SYN, (8)4010.0
ECTL4   SYN, (8)4011.0
EQAV1   SYN, (8)4012.0
EQAV2   SYN, (8)4013.0
EQAV3   SYN, (8)4014.0
EQAV4   SYN, (8)4015.0
EQAV5   SYN, (8)4016.0
EQAV6   SYN, (8)4017.0
EQAV7   SYN, (8)4020.0
EDCP1   SYN, (8)4000.0

! ---- PDF p.129: 51 entries ----------------------------------------
EBAUTO  SYN, ECTL1
